{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Behold, I am sending against you… the swarm (הערוב).</b> You will not find in any of the plagues that Scripture mentions the plague with the definite article ה, and Scripture should have said 'הנני משליח בך ערוב' — behold, I am sending against you a swarm. But this swarm was not a new creation; rather, it was a plague sent to unleash upon them the swarm (ערוב) that was in the wilderness, in the manner of what is written of an evil decree, ״ושלחתי בכם את חית השדה״. And what Scripture mentioned above concerning the frogs — ״בכל גבולך״ — was likewise not a new creation, for they came up from the waters and swarmed from the Nile, one upon another." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> 'הנני משליח בך את הערוב' — It is the way of the world that when flesh and blood seeks to bring harm upon his enemy, he brings it upon him suddenly, so that he will not be aware of it. But the Holy One, blessed be He, is not so: He warns him each and every time concerning every single plague, as it says, ״הנני משליח בך״, ״הנה יד ה' הויה במקנך״, ״הנני נוגף״, ״הנני ממטיר״, ״הנני מביא מחר״, and so for all the plagues. And this is what Scripture says (Job 36:22): ״הן אל ישגיב בכחו מי כמוהו מורה״ — this is a reply to the wicked before destruction, and if they do not repent, they perish from the world, as it says (ibid.): ״אם ישמעו ויעבדו יכלו ימיהם בטוב ושניהם בנעימים״, and ״אם לא ישמעו בשלח יעברו״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:02.799275666Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}